{title: Witness Against You}
{subtitle: Deuteronomy 31:22–30}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Moses wrote the song that day
He taught the people what to say
[Gm]The Lord spoke to Joshua son of Nun
Be strong and brave, the work is done
[Bb]I will bring them into the land
I swore to give with my own hand
[Gm]I myself shall be with you there
No [Eb]fear shall cloud your solemn care
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Take this [Bb]Book of the Law
Place it by [F/A]the ark forev[Gm]er
It stands as a [Eb]witness against [Bb]you
For I [F]know your hearts are [Gm]few
Rebellious and [Eb]stiff-necked is your [Bb]way
Even [F]now in my life to[Bb]day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When the writing was finished completely
From the first verse to the final [Gm]beat
He gave the command to the Le[Eb]vite
Who carries the ark of God's [Bb]light
Place it beside the covenant seat
There it will remain in the street
A [Gm]witness against you, the people see
[Eb]How much more when I am free
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Take this [Bb]Book of the Law
Place it by [F]the ark forev[Gm]er
It stands as a [Eb]witness against [Bb]you
For I [F]know your hearts are [Gm]few
Rebellious and [Eb]stiff-necked is your [Bb]way
Even [F]now in my life to[Bb]day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
As[Gm]semble before me all the elders
[Eb]With the officials and tribal leaders
[Bb]So I may speak these words aloud
And [F]call heaven and earth to crowd
To [Gm]testify against your rebellion
[Eb]Before my death and final [F]fall
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I [Bb]know you will become corrupt
And turn from the path you must
In days to come disaster will come
Because you will do evil, hum
[Gm]Evil in the sight of the Lord
And [Eb]anger Him with what you form
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Take this [Bb]Book of the Law
Place it by the [F]ark forev[Gm]er
It stands as a [Eb]witness against [Bb]you
For I [F]know your hearts are [Gm]few
Rebellious and [Eb]stiff-necked is your [Bb]way
Even [F]now in my life to[Bb]day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Moses recited the song then
[Eb]From the beginning [F7sus4]to the [Bb]end
{end_of_verse}
